{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422699-can-the-dynasty-cooperate-against-an-invasion","id":1422699,"title":"Can the Dynasty cooperate against an invasion?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-11-08T23:48:21-08:00","id":1422699,"title":"Can the Dynasty cooperate against an invasion?","content":"In the thread about when an Anathema would become a serious threat to the Realm, it was opined that in the face of a serious threat, the Houses would mutually agree to ignore their cold war in favor of the hot one on the doorstep. I'm not convinced. <br /> First, there are no Imperial legions anymore, only House legions. That inherently makes any deployment of troops into an intensely political act, with Houses seeking glory but trying to avoid serious danger. '<br /> Second, the central command of the legions has been gutted. Of the nine Crown Marshals in RY 763, two were executed, one is locked up, and the rest in hiding. At best, the one's in hiding might be willing to ignore the insult paid to them in favor of the immediate external threat. More likely, House Iselsi has seven willing and able recruits who are absolutely down for some Vendetta. <br /> Third, this is almost the archtypical prisoner's dilemma. If even one House chooses to strike while it's fellows are fighting the beastfolk armies of Solar Queen Perfect Soul, then the whole resistance will collapse. And since every Dynast will recognize this, no House will cooperate. <br /> Fourth, beyond just the legions, the Realm as a whole has basically no central leadership. The closest is Tepet Fokuf, who is: male, a Tepet post-Futile Blood, most well known for masturbating to Immaculate texts/possibly getting attacked by the Throne itself, and is probably not an Eclipse in disguise. Past him, you have the Deliberative, which.... yeah. <br /> <br /> All told, it's almost more likely that an existential threat to the Realm as a whole would trigger a short, bloody RCW, with someone trying to take the Imperial City and Imperial Manse, to try and quickly claim the Throne and lead the defense. If successful, this would likely result in RCW2 not long after the victory. Although in a Dragon-Blooded campaign, I could easily see an arc where the PCs negotiate an interim leader to stave off the RCW until after the invasion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho","name":"GhanjRho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1424_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T01:05:24-08:00","id":1422706,"title":"","content":"Well how big an external threat is somewhat important. Maha launching an invasion would certainly get a response and his forces can cause a lot of damage, but under the normal situation he wouldn't merit putting everything aside. Just a sort of teeth-clenched teamwork scenario where a number of houses offer assistance and are cautiously accepted or refused based on the capabilities in the area of the invasion. <br /> <br /> Whereas something like the Balorean Crusade represents an existential threat to most of Creation, Realm included, consequently while the Realm might at first not put everything aside after the scale is understood then you would have a mix of those attempting to fight the invasion because its necessary with the odd desperate attempts at reclaiming control of the Imperial Manse to make use of its abilities to you know save all their lives as the priority over being able to use it as a means to gain control of the Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T01:51:59-08:00","id":1422710,"title":"","content":"The Realm will do whatever they are required to do to tell the story your table wants to tell.<br /> <br /> That might be everyone unanimously accepting Mnemon as Empress. It might be everyone backstabbing each other as Rome burns. It might be anything in-between.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-09-2020, 04:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T04:43:09-08:00","id":1422725,"title":"","content":"Hey hey hey. I'm the guy who said they'd engage in jolly cooperation. I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3400_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3400\" data-vbnamecard=\"3400\">nalak42</a> , there's a certain timeless human quality to uniting squabbling factions in the face of an outsider threat. You probably won't get V'Neef and Peleps to work together unless you attack them both simultaneously, but for everyone else, I mean, how perfectly suited to the type of stories Exalted draws from to say &quot;let us set aside our differences to defeat the Demon-Soul Invaders&quot;. Realpolitik is definitely a thing in Creation and the real world, but there's still the foundation of Pragmatism- even the seediest backroom dealers realize that if the Solars take the Jade Throne its going to be the end of their wretched lives. Not to mention the countless do-gooder heroes, the monks upholding their vows, the blood brothers(sisters), and the opportunists. Nothing brings people together like an outsider to hate. <br /> That said, there's still a lot of room for say, House Cathak to &quot;arrive late&quot; to a battle and for another house to be absolutely screwed over, but in the grander context I'd see them working together out of necessity, especially when the first major battles are lost to the Golden Horde. Nobody gets to be king of the Ashes. <br /> <br /> Also I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> , the setting is basically starts the second the wheel comes off the truck so each table can do anything they want. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T04:59:57-08:00","id":1422727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422699-can-the-dynasty-cooperate-against-an-invasion?p=1422725#post1422725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">even the seediest backroom dealers realize that if the Solars take the Jade Throne its going to be the end of their wretched lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the caveat of course that they have to be made aware that the threat of the returning Solars is real. Some prominent folks in the Realm are likely sufficiently insulated from what's going on in the Threshold to not be convinced that the tales of Anathema overturning satrapies isn't just an excuse made by Dynasts who just weren't crushing the populace hard enough.<br /> <br /> \u200b(That said, don't go sending seven guys out to take one captive to show your sister. Or at least target one who's not in the middle of a goddamned army.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-09-2020, 06:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T09:39:30-08:00","id":1422763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422699-can-the-dynasty-cooperate-against-an-invasion?p=1422725#post1422725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, there's still a lot of room for say, House Cathak to &quot;arrive late&quot; to a battle and for another house to be absolutely screwed over, but in the grander context I'd see them working together out of necessity, especially when the first major battles are lost to the Golden Horde.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny that you use the term Golden Horde when that's the historical name of a successor state to Genghis Khan's empire which made significant early strides owing directly to the fact that the Chinese Song Dynasty refused to come to the aid of the northern enemy Jin Dynasty who was the first target of the Mongols. Something which set the stage for the later Mongol conquest of China.<br /> <br /> It's at least as timeless for polities that already have their own conflicts to fail to come together in the face of external threats due to things like insurmountable differences, an assessment that they'd be better spent prioritizing their own border defence, or actively wanting to see this terrifying new threat destroy people that they have a more active hatred for. People often fail to act in what should look like their best self-interest.<br /> <br /> JohnDoe's answer is the most correct one of course in that it's plausible to run the setting either way according to the scenario best suited for the game, but I'd argue the trajectory of the written setting inclines more towards the Houses failing to pull together.<br /> <br /> Although I do think the most engaging way to run that in a game is to have them be on the fence about it and encourage the player characters to actively undermine unity.<br /> <br /> Conversely, the Realm is a playable thing. You can play as characters who see the writing on the wall and then need to actively work to get everybody on the same page, with the likely prospect that they won't on their own forming the stakes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T15:22:34-08:00","id":1422828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422699-can-the-dynasty-cooperate-against-an-invasion?p=1422763#post1422763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's funny that you use the term Golden Horde when that's the historical name of a successor state to Genghis Khan's empire which made significant early strides owing directly to the fact that the Chinese Song Dynasty refused to come to the aid of the northern enemy Jin Dynasty who was the first target of the Mongols. Something which set the stage for the later Mongol conquest of China.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally intentional, I'm a big fan of EU4. Also it just has the perfect ring to it. <br /> <br /> Also, tvtropes calls the thing I'm describing the &quot;Genghis Gambit&quot;, so there's double precedent. Its what Bull of the North is doing more or less, so its happening in game as well","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T15:44:16-08:00","id":1422833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422699-can-the-dynasty-cooperate-against-an-invasion?p=1422828#post1422828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, tvtropes calls the thing I'm describing the &amp;quot;Genghis Gambit&amp;quot;, so there's double precedent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. In more than a decade with TV Tropes, I've managed to miss this one.<br /> <br /> {reads into it}<br /> <br /> That's just bad history, and a poor real world example to match this fictional device to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T15:48:12-08:00","id":1422834,"title":"","content":"&quot;<i>I never thought I\u2019d die fighting side by side with an Ragara.<br /> How about side by side with a friend?<br /> Aye. I could do that.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> ... If you want! Or not. (As John says, basically)<br /> <br /> In general I incline to the idea that the Great Houses probably would close ranks against an outsider, mostly. Ultimately the worldview is based on Dragonblooded hegemony and the Immaculate Philosophy and that takes precedence, and it's mostly &quot;<i>Me against my brother, my brother and I against my cousin, and all of us against the stranger.</i>&quot; and &quot;<i>Fredo, you're my older brother, and I love you. But don't ever take sides with anyone against the Family again. Ever</i>.&quot; (swap some gender nomenclature about for the 3e Realm's more typical analogy).<br /> <br /> It probably wouldn't be efficient cooperation though, not by a long shot; there's going to be lots of score settling and jockeying for position. And whether the rest of the Isle society would play along is entirely uncertain. And this is all very much &quot;<i>At first</i>&quot; - whether this would hold through a bad tactical situation and some defections, or credible rumours of defections that are deliberate, sorcerous empowered *lies*, is much less certain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T22:12:00-08:00","id":1422871,"title":"","content":"Sorry, SOverlord, I was thinking about this during work yesterday, and couldn't find who uttered it when i skimmed the thread before making this one. <br /> <br /> And basically, what Isator said. For all that a common enemy can do wonders to bring foes together, history (and fiction) have all too many examples of people choosing to strike when the enemy is distracted. House Peleps might well accept a deal to stay out of an invasion in exchange for their Western Empire, for example. And my read of the politics of the Dynasty, especially considering the civil war that's brewing, is that they will tend to be more dagger-in-hand or coin-in-hand than hand-in-hand. Consider the Sesus betrayal of Tepet. Tens of thousands of troops and hundreds of Dragon-Blooded were maneuvered to their deaths at the hands Bull of the North. So Sesus could grab more satrapies, and kneecap a rival House. <br /> <br /> Though this does make me imagine a scenario where the Deliberative responds to an immanent invasion by making the Roseblack Regent. Skilled enough to lead the Realm to victory, but from the weakest House, so she can be easily overthrown when the fighting's done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho","name":"GhanjRho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1424_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T23:33:08-08:00","id":1422874,"title":"","content":"I see no reason why they shouldn't cooperate with one another. Ignoring the fact that this depends on every game, there's also the fact that there's no longer any Empress around to keep them at each other's throats. There's now no force setting them against one another. With the Empress no longer playing them against each other, there can now be more chances of cooperation and long-term alliances.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GhanjRho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422699-can-the-dynasty-cooperate-against-an-invasion#post1422699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third, this is almost the archtypical prisoner's dilemma. If even one House chooses to strike while it's fellows are fighting the beastfolk armies of Solar Queen Perfect Soul, then the whole resistance will collapse. And since every Dynast will recognize this, no House will cooperate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Besides, isn't teamwork and brotherhood literally one of the Dragonblooded themes? There is a charm in 2e called 'Ten thousand Dragons fight as one' that lets you automatically create an intimacy of loyalty towards another Dragonblooded in the vicinity. Why can't the DBs have charms and abilities that let them overcome mistrust, so that they can unite against a greater foe? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T01:05:17-08:00","id":1422883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422699-can-the-dynasty-cooperate-against-an-invasion?p=1422874#post1422874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see no reason why they shouldn't cooperate with one another.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Battle of Futile Blood, everything Ragara has done starting with &quot;trying to murder Mnemon in her youth&quot; through owning the majority of debts, and everybody (but especially Sesus) stomping over Nellens spring to mind. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">there's also the fact that there's no longer any Empress around to keep them at each other's throats. There's now no force setting them against one another.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then Peleps asks for V'neef to return tribute transportation rights to them. After all, they were only given away as a tactic by the Empress to create division, it's only fair.<br /> <br /> It's reductive to portray the Empress as only a source of division and as the only source of division.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, isn't teamwork and brotherhood literally one of the Dragonblooded themes?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is. That lends additional dramatic irony to the number of institutional factors and interpersonal beefs that lead to significant infighting among them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Why can't the DBs have charms and abilities that let them overcome mistrust, so that they can unite against a greater foe? <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's not really the intent of the game's dramatic functions or human portrayals for people to have the option to just resolve their personality issues with magic.<br /> <br /> As there's no Charms to govern with wisdom and conscientiousness, there's no switch you can install in yourself to flip to stop being an asshole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T02:00:16-08:00","id":1422886,"title":"","content":"You can be an asshole.<br /> <br /> You can be foolish. <br /> <br /> But nothing stops you from making magic backed Brotherhood pacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T05:42:39-08:00","id":1422898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422699-can-the-dynasty-cooperate-against-an-invasion?p=1422886#post1422886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can be an asshole.<br /> <br /> You can be foolish. <br /> <br /> But nothing stops you from making magic backed Brotherhood pacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on whether or not one proposes to do so with people who don't tolerate fools and assholes.<br /> <br /> Sure Sworn Kinships are depicted as an institution that distinctly crosses party lines, and there's even some foundation to the idea that unity can ultimately arise from networking Hearths together. But it's a bit odd to insist that Hearths being a thing means that the Scarlet Dynasty as a whole pulling together in mutual self-interest is a certainty.<br /> <br /> For one thing, Kinships across different Houses are capable of being a source of tension over loyalties divided between Hearth mates and House elders. Consider the signature character from Lookshy who has trouble with the fact that he won't exploit his Hearth for his home's intelligence gathering. A single Lookshy Exalt forming a bond with some Dynasts doesn't mean that Lookshy and the Realm have no basis for being enemies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T12:13:58-08:00","id":1422935,"title":"","content":"You know, I wonder if I'm simply bad at communicating or my feel and vision of exalted is so different it's like talking about 2 different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T13:27:08-08:00","id":1422949,"title":"","content":"Something to bear in mind with questions like this is that there really isn't going to be one &quot;right answer&quot; that can be established. Saying &quot;people will behave in this manner for sure!&quot; goes against both reality (where people have free will, and can choose paths other than the most likely one), <i>and</i> good setting design (where you want enough freedom and flexibility in the world building that every chronicle can have a slightly different answer).<br /> <br /> So, pretty much every possibility between the two extremes of &quot;the Great Houses are still fighting each other even as the Renewed Deliberative plants its flags in the Imperial City and atop Mount Meru&quot; and &quot;The Great Houses and every outcaste Dragonblood in the Threshold immediately closes ranks and takes a unified stance the moment a Solar or Lunar declares that they're planning to invade&quot; is at least vaguely plausible. <br /> <br /> Of course, the <i>most likely</i> outcome is probably somewhere between those two extremes. Exactly how it actually happens depends greatly on the circumstances of the external threat, and, even more importantly, on the actions of the <i>protagonists of the story</i>, i.e. the PCs. The latter should be the biggest determinant of how things go down. A Circle of Dragonblooded should be able to overcome their families' factionalism and dislike of each other and get them to band together against the looming Anathema threat, or decide to take full advantage of the chaos, let the invasion happen, and then rally scattered DB forces to turn it back and set themselves up as the new Shoguns, Empresses, or whatever title they want. And a circle of Solars, Lunars, etc. should be able to carefully conceal their true nature long enough that the Great Houses don't realize that this is an <i>Anathema</i> invasion until after they've spent themselves on civil war, or use subterfuge and trickery and honest diplomacy to make some Great Houses think others are on the Anathema side, and exploit the civil war that way.<br /> <br /> In the absence of PC actions, though, I think the Great Houses' reactions, and whether they're willing to cooperate with each other or backstab, will depend on exactly how blatant the Anathema are in being behind the invasion. If the Bull of the North recovered tomorrow, and started conquering his way southwest towards Pneuma or straight south to Medo, and makes statements about how he plans to cross the sea and crush the Realm, most of the Houses would probably publicly put aside their differences, though some of them would probably at least think about trying to pull another Battle of Futile Blood on a different House. But since all the Houses are aware of the potential of that, and there's nobody to just command one of them to take the brunt, that's not as likely to be doable. <br /> <br /> Conversely, if an Anathema is more quiet, doesn't proclaim their true nature while building up a power base (or even if they <i>do</i> declare it openly, if their new empire is sufficiently far enough away from the Blessed Isle that they can't get there for a few decades), the Great Houses will probably focus more on defeating each other than fighting the Anathema threat.<br /> <br /> Another factor to think about in deciding whether the Realm unites against an Anathema threat or not is that this is 3e, and Dragon-Blooded are absolutely <i>not</i> pushovers or too weak to challenge &quot;real&quot; Exalted or anything like that. The Dragon-Bloods of the First Age were able to overthrow and imprison the Solars at the height of their power, slay a great many of the similarly-powerful Lunars, and force the rest back to the borders of Creation and keep them hiding in the shadows for centuries. Sure, the Wyld Hunt likes to kill Anathema as early as they can. But that's not because there's some kind of ticking clock of &quot;if we don't off them before Essence 3, we literally can't do anything about them&quot;. The Realm, Lookshy, etc. can all reasonably look at the situation, even now with the return of the Solars, and say &quot;we can wait a few months or years to deal with this problem, because right now, we've got bigger problems closer to home, with all the other Dragon-Blooded trying to kill me&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T13:59:52-08:00","id":1422954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422699-can-the-dynasty-cooperate-against-an-invasion?p=1422949#post1422949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another factor to think about in deciding whether the Realm unites against an Anathema threat or not is that this is 3e, and Dragon-Blooded are absolutely <i>not</i> pushovers or too weak to challenge &quot;real&quot; Exalted or anything like that. The Dragon-Bloods of the First Age were able to overthrow and imprison the Solars at the height of their power, slay a great many of the similarly-powerful Lunars, and force the rest back to the borders of Creation and keep them hiding in the shadows for centuries. Sure, the Wyld Hunt likes to kill Anathema as early as they can. But that's not because there's some kind of ticking clock of &quot;if we don't off them before Essence 3, we literally can't do anything about them&quot;. The Realm, Lookshy, etc. can all reasonably look at the situation, even now with the return of the Solars, and say &quot;we can wait a few months or years to deal with this problem, because right now, we've got bigger problems closer to home, with all the other Dragon-Blooded trying to kill me&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. this. <br /> <br /> Look, I don't know about anyone, but I never liked this shit. Casually backhanding a government is the kind of thing that happens when the person doing it is a Solar and the government is mortal. The Realm rules over an area the size of America, a literal continent on its own. It has one of the highest amounts of Dragonblooded in the world, all of them whom at the very least are trained to lead troops in battle. They have incredible numbers of artifacts, manses, sorcerous workings, and an immense number of soldiers. And that applies to individual houses. <br /> <br /> Like, I get it. People want to easily smash the Realm so they can do things like fuck off to fight the Deathlords and other spiritual existence thing. But can we at least note the fact that for the majority of the DBs in the Realm, they strongly and firmly believe the Solar Exalted would destroy the world and eat their souls? Not to mention the fact that the Solars would very likely supplant and topple their place as rules of the world. People bring up how some people will backstab one another for gain even when threatened by a larger outside foe. But there's nothing that quite promotes solidarity in the noble classes than the idea that they will lose their influence and power. Not to mention probably their lives and souls. <br /> <br /> I repeat. The Solars are a threat to DB hegemony. Yes, Peles can fight against Sesus or Mnemon tries to murder Ragara. But they all kinda realize that they can lose a few vineyards, manses, or shipping companies, or they can risk losing *<i><b>everything</b></i>* instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T15:00:42-08:00","id":1422965,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a>, hmm... Yeees... buutt...<br /> <br /> That kind of thing where there is an idea that previous editions treated the Realm as an easily defeated foe before the &quot;real bad guys turn up&quot; is mostly a meme coined by Holden that combines<br /> <br /> 1) wanting to upsell his (and John's) vision of Ex3 with conflict between the imperialistic Realm and the Solars and Lunars<br /> 2) exploiting fan dissatisfaction with how 2e &quot;dissed&quot; Dragonblooded and focus on &quot;cosmic power&quot; to achieve overmentioned upselling<br /> (He was and probably still is a good salesman/memelord!).<br /> <br /> I don't think people in prior editions, relative to 3e, generally actually played out the conflict between the Realm and Solars as, y'know, the Solars just whomp the Realm trivially and then focus on the &quot;real opposition&quot;... So much as it's more like the Realm is more pre-occupied with internal struggles, and anyway had a lighter, looser and more tenuous hold on much of the Threshold anyway, and is less the overwhelming opponent that Solars are all focused on (and yeah the Deathlords and so on possibly a bit more present).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T15:24:27-08:00","id":1422973,"title":"","content":"I understand what you're saying <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"929\" data-vbnamecard=\"929\">Ghosthead</a> and I admit that I am not the first person who's very astute in social situations. <br /> <br /> But can we at least agree that nothing makes rich, powerful, privileged people cooperate faster than the thought that they might no longer be rich, poweful, and influential?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T15:40:56-08:00","id":1422976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422699-can-the-dynasty-cooperate-against-an-invasion?p=1422973#post1422973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But can we at least agree that nothing makes rich, powerful, privileged people cooperate faster than the thought that they might no longer be rich, poweful, and influential?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on how far in the future the threat is, and how well they think their money can insulate them from the threat. We <i>know</i> a climate disaster is coming, but rather than tighten their belts <i>even a little</i>, the world's wealthiest humans are looking into means to employ slave-soldiers to protect their capital against the people whose lives will be ruined by the disaster said wealthy people caused. They'd literally rather gamble on their ability to either escape to outer space, or, failing that, to climb to the top of the pile in a <i>Mad Max</i> future than <i>live with slightly less</i>.<br /> <br /> This is why my earlier post suggests <i>making</i> the threat real to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T16:01:23-08:00","id":1422980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422699-can-the-dynasty-cooperate-against-an-invasion?p=1422976#post1422976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on how far in the future the threat is, and how well they think their money can insulate them from the threat. We <i>know</i> a climate disaster is coming, but rather than tighten their belts <i>even a little</i>, the world's wealthiest humans are looking into means to employ slave-soldiers to protect their capital against the people whose lives will be ruined by the disaster said wealthy people caused. They'd literally rather gamble on their ability to either escape to outer space, or, failing that, to climb to the top of the pile in a <i>Mad Max</i> future than <i>live with slightly less</i>.<br /> <br /> This is why my earlier post suggests <i>making</i> the threat real to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Objection! <br /> <br /> Climate change is relatively impersonal, is slow, over the time, requires large amounts of data and statistical training to recognize, and has interference run on it by oil companies. Anathema, on the other hand, is very personal, is a known threat, has a habit of murdering your families and friends (hello Lunars) and is something that all DBS understand. I.e. a powerful something that's going to try and kill them. <br /> <br /> Climate change requires fucking over many companies and a lot of very rich powerful people and countries, not to mention revamping the energy systems we tend to use. This causes a lot of feet dragging. A lot of it. In this situation, it's a bit different. Yes, sure, maybe you lose a few lucrative trade deals and maybe you lose a fleet to V'neef. But you're still majorly rich and poweful. You aren't losing everything. But if that anathema comes along, you *will* lose a lot more than that. Up to your life. <br /> <br /> And last of all, its quite likely that the Solar arises in the threshold or whatnot, or somewhere the Realm exploits, and is blocking things like an invading Realm force or attempts to annex a rebellious kingdom. In other words, he's the guy cutting into their profits. He's making them live slightly less. In your analogy, it's as if someone told them that there's a motherload of oil and rare earth minerals buried under the sands, but you gotta topple a few kingdoms to get to it. Killing this guy makes them richer. Not poorer","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T16:15:24-08:00","id":1422982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422699-can-the-dynasty-cooperate-against-an-invasion?p=1422980#post1422980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Objection!</div> </div> </div> </div>Overruled.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422699-can-the-dynasty-cooperate-against-an-invasion?p=1422980#post1422980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anathema, on the other hand... is something that all DBS understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excuse me, but most Exalted don't know the Jade Prison broke; most Exalted don't even know the Jade Prison was a thing. For the entirety of the Realm's history the number of Solars <i>across the world</i> at any given time has been less than twenty, and for most of it, likely less than ten. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422699-can-the-dynasty-cooperate-against-an-invasion?p=1422980#post1422980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Climate change requires fucking over many companies and a lot of very rich powerful people and countries...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not near as much as they'd have you think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422699-can-the-dynasty-cooperate-against-an-invasion?p=1422980#post1422980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if that anathema comes along, you *will* lose a lot more than that. Up to your life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again, this isn't proven to them yet. <b>Prove it to them that things are different now.</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422699-can-the-dynasty-cooperate-against-an-invasion?p=1422980#post1422980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And last of all, its quite likely that the Solar arises in the threshold or whatnot, or somewhere the Realm exploits, and is blocking things like an invading Realm force or attempts to annex a rebellious kingdom. In other words, he's the guy cutting into their profits.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, he's cutting into <i>their competitor's</i> profits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422699-can-the-dynasty-cooperate-against-an-invasion?p=1422980#post1422980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In your analogy, it's as if someone told them that there's a motherload of oil and rare earth minerals buried under the sands, but you gotta topple a few kingdoms to get to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please don't try and tell me how my analogy works. Killing the Solar doesn't increase your wealth; his blood isn't made of jade.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422699-can-the-dynasty-cooperate-against-an-invasion?p=1422980#post1422980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Killing this guy makes them richer. Not poorer</div> </div> </div> </div>No, killing this guy means <i>they've sunk a significant investment into protecting an asset</i>. They're blowing a ton of cash just on the off-chance that it succeeds and they can maintain the status quo.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T17:51:59-08:00","id":1423000,"title":"","content":"Well I guess that's that<br /> <br /> I'm done with this argument","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T18:44:33-08:00","id":1423005,"title":"","content":"Once again, I'm not saying the Dynasty can't, or won't, cooperate against the threat of the returned Solars. Or really any other invaders. But <i>as long as they are not made to confront the reality of the threat</i>, they won't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T18:55:05-08:00","id":1423008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422699-can-the-dynasty-cooperate-against-an-invasion?p=1423005#post1423005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again, I'm not saying the Dynasty can't, or won't, cooperate against the threat of the returned Solars. Or really any other invaders. But <i>as long as they are not made to confront the reality of the threat</i>, they won't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look man. <br /> <br /> Looking at the the context, entirety of the thread, as well as what we know of Exalted...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In the thread about when an Anathema would become a serious threat to the Realm, it was opined that in the face of a serious threat, the Houses would mutually agree to ignore their cold war in favor of the hot one on the doorstep. I'm not convinced.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> First, there are no Imperial legions anymore, only House legions. That inherently makes any deployment of troops into an intensely political act, with Houses seeking glory but trying to avoid serious danger. '<br /> </div> </div> </div>For this scenario, I'm positing that this entire thing has snowballed out of control. The Realms legions have been battered, like half a dozen battles of Futile Blood. There are records and sightings of dozens if not hundreds of Anathema. Numerous satrapies are already in full on rebellion with the resulting massacre of Realm Citizens and Dragonblooded who are sent to quell the riots. The Threshold is lost. And on the other side of the sea, a fleet of ships are already being built, ready to attack the Blessed Isle, with legions of Tiger Warriors on board of them. <br /> <br /> It is that level of rebellion that has shaken the Realm. A full on invasion fleet about to strike at the center of the world. <br /> <br /> It's not that they can't ignore the threat of the returned solars. It's that if the Anathema are any serious threat and are massing a strike to attack the Imperial Capital, they would probably capitulate and figure out that yes, now is the time to make peace with others. Because when an entire army of Anathema are marching down on the doorsteps, it gets rather difficult. <br /> <br /> How many houses extract things from the threshold? How many have Satrapies? How many will have their supply of slaves/ drugs/ metal/ plants/ grain/ jade cut off from them? How many of them will send in the house legions which will then get murdered? How many will look at an army of encroaching Anathema, the loss of their Satrapies, the defeat of their House Legions, and think: &quot;I think this isn't too important.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T19:38:28-08:00","id":1423013,"title":"","content":"There's a couple of other players in the game as well. The Deathlords have tipped their hand with Thorns for one, that complicates things a lot. From the Dynasty side an unstoppable undead force lead by some kind of dead-anathema just punked one of their satrapies and made a cloak from the skinned terrestrial defenders. On the other hand though the returning Solars might look between the Realm and Thorns and decide the Realm can wait because that Mask of Winters guy and his dozen Abyssal Exalted are more concerning. So it might be really big in making the Dynasty stand up, or it might be a distraction that blunts the blow of returning Solars.<br /> <br /> Which goes for a lot of things too. Currently most satrapies aren't in Solar hands, they're in Dynasty hands, but with their garrisons largely emptying for the Isle. The Solars might strike to take one, but that one might have an Infernal working some cultist magic, so they can't really strike out at the Isle from there because their roots will rot away while they do. Or, hell, maybe two groups of Solars both contest that satrapy. Some group comes in to bail out Perfect Soul and take Jiara, but since they came to bail her out they kinda feel like maybe they should be in charge.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the whole though, the Realm sponsors a global state religion that targets the Solars and Lunars as Anathema, so on balance I imagine they're going to be unified against the Realm more than fighting eachother or the other powers. It's just that they don't show up and immediately band together with the Lunars and go storming the Blessed Isle necessarily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T20:13:16-08:00","id":1423018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422699-can-the-dynasty-cooperate-against-an-invasion?p=1423000#post1423000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I guess that's that<br /> <br /> I'm done with this argument</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">I'm banning you for a day due to the fact you seem to be having serious issues dropping into threads and getting upset with fellow posters.<br /> <br /> If you're not having fun, don't post.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T23:28:22-08:00","id":1423193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422699-can-the-dynasty-cooperate-against-an-invasion?p=1422982#post1422982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overruled.<br /> <br /> <br /> Excuse me, but most Exalted don't know the Jade Prison broke; most Exalted don't even know the Jade Prison was a thing. For the entirety of the Realm's history the number of Solars <i>across the world</i> at any given time has been less than twenty, and for most of it, likely less than ten.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll be frank with you. <br /> <br /> Given the entirety of this thread, this entire post, this entire thing, this entire knowledge of the Exalted line, especially considering what is considering being asked here: <br /> <br /> Do you think that there's 10 solar now, or 100 of them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T00:14:45-08:00","id":1423203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422699-can-the-dynasty-cooperate-against-an-invasion?p=1423193#post1423193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the entirety of this thread, this entire post, this entire thing, this entire knowledge of the Exalted line, especially considering what is considering being asked here: <br /> <br /> Do you think that there's 10 solar now, or 100 of them?</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s more than a hundred; <b>that said</b> - how many do you think a single Dynast (at the top level of decision-making power in her House) is concretely aware of? How many do you think she\u2019s assuming are just misreported God-Blooded, or wild peasant tales given too much credence by overzealous Immaculates like Deled? How many do you think she\u2019s got the time and manpower to investigate before spreading herself too thin? How many family members do you think she\u2019s willing to send to their possible deaths to check out a rumor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-12-2020, 03:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T00:34:45-08:00","id":1423205,"title":"","content":"Didn't the OP say 'in the face of a serious threat'? <br /> <br /> To be honest in the case of what the OP said, the threat is obvious, large, and very much 'in your face'. Because beastfolk armies were mentioned. Since I read the OP, I presume that he meant 'Yeah, the Realm knows about the threat about to come crashing down, but is that enough to get them to work together?'. Not 'The realm doesn't know about the threat and is too bothered by infighting and too dumb to figure it out'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T00:44:40-08:00","id":1423208,"title":"","content":"Again with this dichotomy. Dumb is not the same as unaware. Having been lied to or given bad information does not make you stupid. Not realizing one\u2019s biases is something all of us do. The Exalted are human, and the mistakes they make are human mistakes.<br /> <br /> Given current events, it\u2019s very easy to misjudge a serious threat, and thus not react appropriately to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T01:00:30-08:00","id":1423212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422699-can-the-dynasty-cooperate-against-an-invasion?p=1423208#post1423208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again with this dichotomy. Dumb is not the same as unaware. Having been lied to or given bad information does not make you stupid. Not realizing one\u2019s biases is something all of us do. The Exalted are human, and the mistakes they make are human mistakes.<br /> <br /> Given current events, it\u2019s very easy to misjudge a serious threat, and thus not react appropriately to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, here's the thing. <br /> <br /> How much of this is going to happen? <br /> <br /> I'm not denying that they're certainly very imperfect. But how much bias, how much bad information, and how much lying? And most of all, how much of it before they get shouted down by 'yes, the anathema are here and we're going to die unless we team up!'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T01:40:24-08:00","id":1423215,"title":"","content":"Is anyone trying to argue that the Dynasty <b>definitely can't</b> or <b>definitely will </b>unite to fight the Anathema?<br /> <br /> Because if anyone is taking an absolute position, I'm happy to debate it. (Either side, I don't mind.)<br /> <br /> But if we're arguing about what individuals think is most likely... <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pWdd6_ZxX8c\" target=\"_blank\">well, that's just, like, your opinion man</a>.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't think the Realm is Lawful Stupid, and I lean toward agreeing with Accelerator. But it's not a guaranteed thing: people aren't rational actors (even before Essence Fever and the Great Curse and 768 years of internal strife). &quot;A person is smart, people are dumb, panicky animals.&quot; It is demonstratable that people don't always act in their best interests.<br /> <br /> But rather than talk about climate change, let's look at stuff like the World Wars. Heck, Russia and the US united long enough to crush Daesh in all our lifetimes. Folks <b>will </b>set aside differences and work against a common threat. Ignorance plays a factor, and the Realm hasn't united yet -- despite Thorns, and the disappearance of the Empress, and the Bull of the North. It is <b>absolutely</b> plausible that they never unite (for all the reasons listed in the OP). The actions of a plucky group of PCs can make all the difference. But is anyone saying that uniting with your sisters against a common threat is impossible?<br /> <br /> Should a group of Anathema cut out the Realm's knees by conquering the Threshold, I think the Dynasty will continue to squabble like the Empire of Trantor as they're dragged into the long night. But if a group of Anathema directly attacked the Blessed Isle, openly as an immediate threat... they face Ten Thousand Dragons, united in opposition. In my opinion. Your Mileage May Vary. Do what is fun at your table. What are we even arguing about here? Neither extreme (nor any middle ground) is Bad Wrong Fun. Just enjoy Exalted, folks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T05:19:54-08:00","id":1423241,"title":"","content":"I was not saying that unity is impossible - merely that it\u2019s not guaranteed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T09:39:08-08:00","id":1423303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1422699-can-the-dynasty-cooperate-against-an-invasion?p=1423215#post1423215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The actions of a plucky group of PCs can make all the difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO this is the most important point.<br /> <br /> If the PCs are Dragonblooded trying to unite the Realm against the threat of the Solars then, well, the Realm is probably going to get united, even if it takes the entire campaign.<br /> <br /> If the PCs are Solars trying to inflame the internal divisions of the Realm using forged evidence of treason, secret alliances, and good-old fashioned persuasion, so that their designs against the Realm can work, then, well...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T12:02:21-08:00","id":1423336,"title":"","content":"This is really up to the Storyteller's interpretation. I could absolutely see as charismatic leader pulling off a temporary alliance to fend off a powerful threat. I could also see the great houses squabbling and trying to gain whatever advantage they could in the situation, leading to chaos. Hell, it is 100% possible that the difference between those two outcomes is dependent on the actions of the PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}